- `1BmveEMNbG.md` (8,8,6,6; Accept) — FO logic characterization of neural link predictors on KGs.
- `sZQRUrvLn4.md` (6,6,6,6,8; Spotlight) — GNN substructure counting, also criticized for restricted scope but accepted.
- `qKgd7RaAem.md` (8,6,6,8; Accept) — fine-grained expressivity via pseudometrics.

Low-end anchors with related weaknesses: `AlkANue4lm.md` (3,5,6,3; Reject) and `3fRbP8g2LT.md` (5,6,3,6; Reject) — both on non-redundant/redundancy-free MPNN expressivity, rejected largely for execution/clarity issues.

The paper under review is a genuinely unifying theoretical contribution with a clean recursive construction, broad applicability within the GACNN paradigm, and a concrete resolution of an open conjecture in homomorphism expressivity. Its weaknesses are primarily clarity/framing (Definition 2 asymmetry, "complete" overreach, missing inline pointers to lower-bound arguments) rather than technical flaws in the core construction. This places it above the rejected anchors but somewhat below the top-tier accepts (`1BmveEMNbG`, `qKgd7RaAem`) because the core claims are presented with less precision about what "equivalence" and the "=" in Corollary 10 actually mean. It is comparable to `FddFxi08J3`.

